// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Attempt 66 (53.3%, best) primary failure: 142 mode_A examples where the model
// generates syntactically correct but semantically wrong SQL. Dominant sub-error:
// adding unrequested columns (e.g., adding "name" when only "age, hometown"
// asked). Secondary: repetition loops from schema-valid repeated tokens.
//
// Changes from attempt 66:
// 1. Guidance: Add explicit "SELECT only the exact columns asked for" instruction
//    targeting the most common mode_A sub-error (extra-column additions).
// 2. Phase 1 preamble: Replace the 5-step UnconstrainedStep loop with a single
//    UnconstrainedChunk(8) call. This lets the model emit "SQL: <<" in one shot
//    more naturally, stopping early at "<<" if it is emitted.
// 3. EnterObservedConstrainedSpan: Use the proper span-entry helper after
//    UnconstrainedChunk reports stoppedOnOpenSpan, matching API contract.
// 4. Phase 3 and Phase 4 identical to attempt 66:
//    RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure(budget=300, retries=5, rollback=50);
//    CloseConstrainedSpan or CloseSpanWithinBudget(120).
//
// Budget ceiling: Phase1(8)+Phase2(1)+Phase3(300)+Phase4(120) = 429 << 900.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 (parser_validity):
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
// Phase 1 (UnconstrainedChunk): Guard is !insideConstrainedOut, so the
//   implication is vacuous on entry to this block. If stoppedOnOpenSpan,
//   EnterObservedConstrainedSpan sets currentConstrainedOut := []; IsValidPrefix([])
//   holds by the method precondition `parser.IsValidPrefix([])`. If not
//   stoppedOnOpenSpan, insideConstrainedOut remains false (vacuous).
//
// Phase 2 (OpenConstrainedSpan): Only runs when !insideConstrainedOut.
//   Postcondition sets currentConstrainedOut := []; IsValidPrefix([]) holds.
//
// Phase 3 (RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure): Helper postcondition guarantees
//   resultConstrained is always parser.IsValidPrefix. Assigning
//   currentConstrainedOut := resultConstrained re-establishes the invariant.
//   insideConstrainedOut unchanged (still true from Phase 2 or entry).
//
// Phase 4a (CloseConstrainedSpan): Sets insideConstrainedOut := false, making
//   the implication vacuously true; clears currentConstrainedOut := [].
//
// Phase 4b (CloseSpanWithinBudget): Postcondition directly guarantees
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
//
// Invariant 2 (progress): |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
// Phase 1: UnconstrainedChunk postcondition: |generatedOut| <= |old generated|
//   + stepsUsed, and stepsUsed <= chunkBudget <= maxSteps - steps_before.
//   After assignment: steps_new = stepsUsed; |generated| = |generatedOut|
//   <= |generatedPrefix| + stepsUsed = |generatedPrefix| + steps_new. ✓
//   EOS tokens count in stepsUsed but are not appended, so length bound holds.
//
// Phase 2: OpenConstrainedSpan appends exactly 1 "<<"; steps += 1. 1:1 ratio.
//
// Phase 3: stablePrefix = generated[..|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|].
//   |new_generated| = |stablePrefix| + |resultConstrained|
//     <= (|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|) + sqlBudget
//     <= |generated| + sqlBudget
//     <= |generatedPrefix| + old_steps + sqlBudget = |generatedPrefix| + new_steps.
//   sqlBudget <= remaining-1 = maxSteps - old_steps - 1 ensures new_steps <= maxSteps.
//   Also |currentConstrainedOut_new| = |resultConstrained| <= |stablePrefix| +
//   |resultConstrained| = |generated_new|, preserving the length sub-invariant. ✓
//
// Phase 4a: CloseConstrainedSpan +1 step, appends at most 1 ">>" token. ≤1:1.
// Phase 4b: CloseSpanWithinBudget postcondition |generatedOut| <= |generated|
//   + closeBudget; steps += closeBudget. Invariant preserved transitively.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
